          <h2>Why I Started SiliconPen</h2>
          <p>
            I’ve always been <em>that guy</em>—the one who explains concepts to friends <strong>5 minutes before an exam</strong>. When I entered college, I noticed a gap: many students struggled with understanding core concepts because the way professors taught <strong>didn’t resonate with them</strong>.
          </p>

          <p>
            People <strong>grasp concepts better when they’re explained by someone who truly understands their struggles</strong>. That’s why I started <strong>SiliconPen</strong>—to make <strong>electronics and circuits simpler</strong> for anyone eager to learn. If even one person benefits from this, it’ll be worth it.
